#X text 685 -1222 == GUI HUB (2026-08-08) == bridge_guiHub is the control surface's way in and out\\\, rebuilding the path the Max patch had through [gate 1] -> [js node.script ws_server.js]\\\, which this conversion dropped. Its 3 outlets feed bridge_slicer\\\, bridge_analyzeReader and analyze_reader -- the SAME inlets the message boxes already use\\\, so it adds no new command paths\\\, only a second way to reach the existing ones. Its inlet takes telemetry going the other way. Run the Node side alongside Pd: node src/gui/gui_hub_bridge.js\\\, then open localhost:8080/panel.html., f 74;
#X text 1782 -650 bridge_slicer's outlets 0 and 1 are TEE'D here\\\, not moved: whatever they already drive is untouched\\\, and the panel gets a copy. Outlet 0 is tagged "status play" on the way out because its playback-trigger form starts with the stem name and has no tag of its own\\\; outlet 1 already tags itself (desc/seg/ready/slices/sysMsg) so it only needs "status" in front. [list trim] converts the list back into a message whose SELECTOR is status\\\, which is what bridge_guiHub's [pd packOSC] turns into the OSC address., f 74;
#X text 2429 847 stem_telemetry~ is listen-only -- it taps the post-gain signal and reports meters/spectrum/RMS to the hub without touching it. The master instance is fed by three [+~] summing the same four stems the dac~ gets\\\, so it measures what you actually hear. Adding or removing any of these cannot change the audio path., f 65;
